# Tests for expressions.sem: one test per invariant (a test may verify the
# invariants of the operations it needs together), each building a small tree
# or table and asserting on what the operations return.

numberTest is test
numberTest purpose "A number node for 42 evaluates to 42"
numberTest verifies addNumber holdsNumber
numberTest verifies evaluate numberIsItself
numberTest typeParameter none
numberTest input none
numberTest output none
numberTest outputOwnedBy none
numberTest raises none
numberTest effect none
numberTest uses none
numberTest memoryHeap true
numberTest async false
numberTest maxRecursion none
numberTest label begin loopKind none
numberTest label begin within none
numberTest label evaluated loopKind none
numberTest label evaluated within none
numberTest label refused loopKind none
numberTest label refused within none
numberTest let fortyTwo Int64 42 immutable
numberTest let refusedText String "a number node was not evaluated" immutable
numberTest at begin do makeNodes
numberTest at begin do makeSymbols
numberTest at begin do addFortyTwo
numberTest at begin do runIt
numberTest at begin branch ifError runIt goto refused else goto evaluated
numberTest at evaluated do expectFortyTwo
numberTest at evaluated return ok none
numberTest at refused do failRefused
numberTest at refused return ok none

store is region
store in numberTest
store strategy arena
store maxBytes 4096
store released atReturn

makeNodes is call
makeNodes in numberTest
makeNodes invokes Nodes.new
makeNodes argument region Region store lend
makeNodes result nodes Nodes
makeNodes ownedBy store
makeNodes cleanedBy none
makeNodes borrows none
makeNodes catch none
makeNodes suppresses none

makeSymbols is call
makeSymbols in numberTest
makeSymbols invokes Symbols.new
makeSymbols argument region Region store lend
makeSymbols result symbolTable Symbols
makeSymbols ownedBy store
makeSymbols cleanedBy none
makeSymbols borrows none
makeSymbols catch none
makeSymbols suppresses none

